      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. The usual prescription dose is 400\u2013800 mg per dose, three to four times daily. Doses this high greatly raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** This tool is for clinicians entering medication orders. A medication order should come from a licensed prescriber who has assessed the patient, not from the finance office.\n\nIf this order is meant for a real patient, please ask the treating prescriber to enter it or confirm it. They may have meant a different dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg, or a different frequency. If a clinician confirms the intended dose, they can send it to me and I can enter it then."
      }
