      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either problem.\n\n- **You're not a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst. A clinician needs to confirm the order, and you can't do that for them.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, double the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter the order right away if the treating prescriber gives me a dose within the standard range. Examples are 800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, or 400 mg every 6 hours.\n- Help you route the request to the prescriber or pharmacy for review.\n\nIf the prescriber really wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves. That should go through the hospital's pharmacist review and override process."
      }
